The query in `1result.sql` is the best choice because  
• it explicitly filters on `do_date = '2014‑01‑01'`, guaranteeing the 2018 5‑year ACS release is used;  
• it limits the search to California tracts (`geo_id LIKE '06%'`);  
• it orders by the income difference and returns exactly one row.  

`0result.sql` is equally correct but adds an unnecessary secondary sort term, while `2result.sql` omits the `do_date` filter, which is risky if additional vintage rows appear later.

```plaintext
1result.sql
```